      <person xml:id="LEP01" sex="1">
         <persName>
            <forename>Benjamin</forename>
            <surname>Lepard</surname>
         </persName>
         <birth when="1000"></birth>
         <death when="1000"></death>
         <occupation>Bookseller</occupation>
         <note type="editorial">
            <p>Benjamin Lepard was insured as a bookseller and stationer in London in 1807, having come from a Baptist family with several booksellers. He appears alongside other literary figures, including <persName key="HOD02">Hodgkins</persName> and was visited by Godwin several times between 1807-08. </p>
            <p>There was no one called Lepard active in the law in 1807 so Benjamin seems the most likely individual here.</p>
         </note>
         <bibl type="website">Ed Pope History (01/08/2018)</bibl>
         <bibl type="other">Wordsworth Trust - Bewick Collection: Benjamin Lepard and Thomas Bewick letters</bibl>
      </person>
